%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: YurIntermission2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118492191588352
    - rid: 1790118492191588353
    - rid: 1790118492191588354
    - rid: 1790118492191588355
    - rid: 1790118492191588356
    - rid: 1790118492191588357
    - rid: 1790118492191588358
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3cb94d3bf4229df4783494bf781bd7f8, type: 2}
    dialog: The existence of so-called "Doomstones" throughout Skyrim has been repeatedly
      verified. The meaning of these stones has not.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118492191588359
    - rid: 1790118492191588360
    - rid: 1790118492191588361
    - rid: 1790118492191588362
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3cb94d3bf4229df4783494bf781bd7f8, type: 2}
    dialog: The prevailing opinion of Skyrim natives is that the stones are indeed
      magical in nature.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3cb94d3bf4229df4783494bf781bd7f8, type: 2}
    dialog: While there is no direct evidence of this, it does seem likely.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3cb94d3bf4229df4783494bf781bd7f8, type: 2}
    dialog: References to similar stones appear in lore throughout the various Tamrielic
      cultures.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3cb94d3bf4229df4783494bf781bd7f8, type: 2}
    dialog: 'None, however, exactly match the markings or distribution of Skyrim''s
      stones. '
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3cb94d3bf4229df4783494bf781bd7f8, type: 2}
    dialog: At present, there is no confirmation of any of the various theories surrounding
      the nature of these stones.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3cb94d3bf4229df4783494bf781bd7f8, type: 2}
    dialog: Their relative positions do not indicate that any individual stone is
      part of a larger, unobserved pattern.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3cb94d3bf4229df4783494bf781bd7f8, type: 2}
    dialog: Also, their placement throughout Skyrim does not correspond to any known
      magical phenomenon.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3cb94d3bf4229df4783494bf781bd7f8, type: 2}
    dialog: The age of these stones has yet to be officially determined; it is widely
      assumed that they were placed during the Merethic era.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3cb94d3bf4229df4783494bf781bd7f8, type: 2}
    dialog: Writings from that period, including those of Ysgramor himself, make
      no mention of the stones and thus this idea cannot be verified.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3cb94d3bf4229df4783494bf781bd7f8, type: 2}
    dialog: Nonetheless, many are drawn to these stones based on the local stories
      describing them as a source of significant power.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3cb94d3bf4229df4783494bf781bd7f8, type: 2}
    dialog: The College will continue to research these intriguing objects, and,
      of course, any findings will be relayed with all possible haste.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118492191588363
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 4c9db5d4425cb424da7340fe5fac55ca, type: 2}
    dialog: These Doomstones, are they related to the Standing Stones?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118492191588365
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3cb94d3bf4229df4783494bf781bd7f8, type: 2}
    dialog: The "Standing Stones" are another name for Doomstones, yes.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 4c9db5d4425cb424da7340fe5fac55ca, type: 2}
    dialog: In that case, it's a bit odd that you didn't mention how each stone is
      engraved with one of the star signs.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6ce26110965197241908f3f9f7ef5410, type: 2}
    dialog: That <i>does</i> seem like a major oversight.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3cb94d3bf4229df4783494bf781bd7f8, type: 2}
    dialog: Indeed, unlike certain Doomstones found in Cyrodiil, the stones in Skyrim
      only feature the insignias of the star signs.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3cb94d3bf4229df4783494bf781bd7f8, type: 2}
    dialog: Unfortunately, this information doesn't help with our understanding of
      the stones; it only adds more questions.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118492191588366
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6ce26110965197241908f3f9f7ef5410, type: 2}
    dialog: Is it possible that these stones were perhaps erected to channel the
      starlight energy from the birth signs to a specific place or purpose here on
      Tamriel?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3cb94d3bf4229df4783494bf781bd7f8, type: 2}
    dialog: Certainly as good a guess as any, but you would be hard pressed to find
      any evidence to prove it.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: (What even <i>are</i> these star signs?)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: (I feel like it would be too awkward to ask at this point in the discussion...)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118492191588367
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions: []
